            <title>[LU-21317] e2image -Q/-r fails for filesystems &gt; 512 TiB: qcow2 L1 table &gt; 2 GiB not written/read</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21317</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a filesystem larger than 512 TiB - 1 GiB (4 KiB blocks) the qcow2 L1 table exceeds 0x7ffff000 bytes (MAX_RW_COUNT, the most a single read()/write() transfers). Both the qcow2 writer and reader in e2image do a single read()/write() of the whole L1 table.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Writer&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;e2image -Q&lt;/tt&gt;): &lt;tt&gt;output_qcow2_meta_data_blocks()&lt;/tt&gt; passes the L1 size to &lt;tt&gt;generic_write(int fd, void *buf, int blocksize, ...)&lt;/tt&gt;. The size is truncated to &lt;tt&gt;int&lt;/tt&gt;:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;0x7ffff000 &amp;lt; size &amp;lt; 2^31: short write, e2image exits with "error in generic_write()";&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;2^31 &amp;lt;= size &amp;lt; 2^32: negative int -&amp;gt; write() fails with EFAULT, nothing written, exit 1;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;size &amp;gt;= 2^32 (fs &amp;gt;= 1 PiB): truncated size may be positive -&amp;gt; L1 table silently written partially, exit 0, corrupted image.&lt;br/&gt;
In all cases the L2 tables and data clusters are already written, so a large qcow2 file with a zeroed/partial L1 table is left behind.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reader&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;e2image -r&lt;/tt&gt;): &lt;tt&gt;qcow2_read_l1_table()&lt;/tt&gt; gets a short read and returns stale errno, e.g.
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;e2image: No such file or directory while trying to convert qcow2 image (fs.raw) into raw image (fs.qcow2)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(the file names in the message are also swapped).&lt;br/&gt;
Even with a fixed reader, an image with a zeroed L1 converts to an empty sparse file.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Limits (max blocks = 268434944 * blocksize/8):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class='table-wrap'&gt;
&lt;table class='confluenceTable'&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;blocksize&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;max blocks&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;max fs size&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;1 KiB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;34,359,672,832&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;32 TiB - 32 MiB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;2 KiB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;68,719,345,664&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;128 TiB - 256 MiB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;4 KiB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;137,438,691,328&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;512 TiB - 1 GiB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Seen with a 513 TiB ldiskfs filesystem (137,759,705,088 4 KiB blocks, L1 table 2,152,495,392 bytes): the 334 GB qcow2 image has an all-zero L1 table and cannot be converted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Fix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;"e2image: handle qcow2 L1 table larger than 2GiB": write and read the L1 table in pieces, return EXT2_ET_SHORT_READ on short L1/L2 reads, fix the swapped file names in the qcow2-to-raw error message.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
